-- title:
--   Adic completeness of the uv=π crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $\hat{\mathcal O}$ be a commutative ring which is local, Noetherian, and complete and separated for its maximal-ideal-adic filtration (i.e. `IsAdicComplete` holds for $\mathfrak m_{\hat{\mathcal O}}$), and let $\pi \in \hat{\mathcal O}$. Write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel` $\hat{\mathcal O}\,\pi$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\hat{\mathcal O}[[X_0,X_1]]$ (formally, `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) Ô`) by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ is viewed as a constant power series. Assume furthermore, as a hypothesis, that $R$ is a local ring. The conclusion is that $R$ is complete and separated for the adic filtration by the powers of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$: every Cauchy sequence for this filtration has a limit, and the intersection of the powers of $\mathfrak m_R$ is zero. Note that the locality of $R$ is assumed rather than derived, and no hypothesis such as $\pi$ being a non-unit or non-zero-divisor is imposed.
--
--   This records that the crossing model $\hat{\mathcal O}[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, the standard local model for a node in the arithmetic setting (e.g. for Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation and for formal neighbourhoods of crossing points on modular curves), satisfies the adic-completeness hypothesis needed for Hensel-type and linearisation arguments. It is used as an instance-level input by numerous statements about automorphisms, deformations and local structure of the crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_isAdicComplete_maximalIdeal.lean

